---
title: Quick milk buns
servings: 12
tags: [baking, bread, quick]
source: https://github.com/LiHRaM/cooklang-recipes
description: Soft buns from a single short rise. Done in the time it takes to lay the table.
---

Dissolve the @fresh yeast{50%g} in the @water{50%ml}(lukewarm) in the bowl of a #stand mixer{}.

Add the @sugar{2%tsp}, @coarse salt{1.5%tsp}, @milk{300%ml}, @butter{50%g}(melted) and @flour{450%g}. Knead with the dough hook until the dough is smooth and elastic.

Shape into twelve buns and set them on a #baking sheet{} lined with baking paper. Cover and let them rise for ~{20%minutes}.

Bake in the #oven{} at 200 °C on the middle rack for ~{18%minutes}, until golden and baked through.

Cool on a wire rack and serve warm or cold.
